## Acknowledgments

The implementation draws on public observations of Cline Pass routing from these MIT-licensed projects:

| Project | Information used |
|---|---|
| [munmunjaklin458-afk/cline-pass-switcher](https://github.com/munmunjaklin458-afk/cline-pass-switcher) | Pipeline identification, planner routing through `providerOptions.gateway`, and provider discovery using `__probe__` |
| [Stabilize7440/cpagw-gateway](https://github.com/Stabilize7440/cpagw-gateway) | Writing both pipeline formats and forwarding unmatched requests without provider injection |
| [yhshzh/dsh-cline-pass](https://github.com/yhshzh/dsh-cline-pass) | Pipeline probing and reading `finalProvider` / `canonicalSlug` from response metadata |

No source code was copied from these projects. The proxy was implemented independently in Go using the observed API behavior. Please open an issue if this attribution needs correction.

Provider discovery avoids inference only when the model honors the injected filter. Models that ignore it may generate a response and incur charges.

## Service access and credentials

Use of Cline Pass and its upstream providers remains subject to their applicable service terms. This proxy forwards client credentials or uses a configured upstream key; configuration files can contain plaintext credentials. It does not provide a separate client authentication layer for ordinary API routes.
